# ── Secrets (never commit) ───────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.pem
*.key

# ── Backups + exports (contain live data) ────────────────────────────
# Both formats: *.sql.gz was the single-database archive, *.tar.gz is the
# current two-database one. These hold every subscription, key prefix and
# usage record in the business — they must never enter a PUBLIC repo.
backup-*.sql.gz
backup-*.tar.gz
latency.csv

# ── Node / Next.js ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
playwright-report/
test-results/
.DS_Store

# ── Local tooling state ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editor/agent workspace markers. Machine-local identity, not project
# content, and this repository is public.
.freebuff/
.claude/

# ── Rust (engine/) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `target/` is ~2GB of build artifacts; committing it would bloat a public
# repo past usability. `Cargo.lock` is NOT ignored: this is an application,
# not a library, so the lockfile is what makes a release build reproducible
# — and engine/Dockerfile copies it deliberately.
target/

# ── Operator scratch (never commit) ───────────────────────────────────
# `_rescue/` holds pg_dump archives of the LIVE portal database plus
# extracted D17 payment evidence — real authorization numbers, sender
# phone numbers, key hashes and the full audit log. The repository is
# PUBLIC, so a `git add -A` here would publish customer and payment data.
# Backups belong off-box; this is a local copy, not project content.
_rescue/

# session state. Anchored to the repo ROOT on purpose: a bare `*.png` would
# also swallow every image asset under portal/public/images/ (mascot, logos,
# app shots — seven are already tracked), so a new marketing asset would
# vanish on `git add` with no error. Root-only catches the scratch shots.
/*.png

# ── Local data (never commit) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# D17 proof screenshots: user-uploaded images. Local/dev only until the
# VPS path is set; they are served read-only to staff, never publicly.
data/

# ── A different product, vendored by accident (never commit) ──────────
# mobile-app/ is a 2.9 GB clone of https://github.com/cogwheel0/conduit
# (its own .git, its own release cadence) sitting inside this repo. It is
# not part of the gateway and nothing here imports it. Committing it would
# add a third-party tree to a PUBLIC repository and would not even be a
# sane submodule — it is a working copy someone dropped here.
#
# It is NOT ignored by any existing rule, so `git add .` would have swept
# 2.9 GB in. That is the kind of mistake that is only noticed at push
# time, after the history is already large.
/mobile-app/

# ── Secrets backups (never commit) ──────────────────────────────────
# .env.bak-codehost is a root-owned copy of the live .env (SMTP, Postgres,
# Resend, upstream keys). Pattern-cousin of .env but not caught by the
# rules above, so it is blocked explicitly.
.env.bak*

# ── Agent/editor workspace state (machine-local, never project) ──────
.verdent/

# ── Halloween banner: source + unreferenced oversized renditions ─────
# Only hero-banner.png / .jpg / .svg are referenced by the site. The rest
# would be ~16MB of dead weight, and public/ is served verbatim.
portal/public/images/halloween/hero-banner-src.pdf
portal/public/images/halloween/hero-banner-3200.png
portal/public/images/halloween/hero-banner-3840.png
